2026-10-09T02:14:05.1128231Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1230932Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1241744Z [0m
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1242593Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1243131Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1243364Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1243938Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1244486Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1244769Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1245026Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1245422Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1245595Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1246403Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1247504Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1248343Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1248939Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1249221Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1249480Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1249738Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1250012Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1250383Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1250509Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1250634Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1250783Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1251166Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1251657Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1258753Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1258938Z I will:
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1259167Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1259528Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1260339Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1261183Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1261606Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1261882Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1262173Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1262597Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1262964Z    /root
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1275842Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1276955Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1288861Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1290003Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1290501Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1291149Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1291903Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1312863Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1313716Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1324286Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1325066Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1325510Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1325837Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1326427Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1326767Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1327056Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1327608Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1328008Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1328203Z If you would like to
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1328710Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1329010Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1329356Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-09T02:14:05.1329953Z   $ sh ./install-nix
